{
    "summary": "Add an order status lifecycle, admin-initiated refunds, and a signed payment-provider webhook, and replace the notify module with a mail module that renders HTML confirmations.",
    "findings": [
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:21",
            "finding": "`requireAdmin` rejects only when the role is neither \"admin\" nor `undefined`, so callers with no role pass the admin check, contrary to its own comment. Anonymous callers can issue refunds through `adminRefund`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:47",
            "finding": "`handlePaymentEvent` verifies the signature only when one is supplied, so a forged `paid` event without a signature marks any order paid. `SECRET` also defaults to \"\" when `PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset, which makes signatures forgeable."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:18",
            "finding": "The customer-typed discount code is interpolated into the HTML mail without `escapeHtml`, unlike the other fields, which allows HTML injection into confirmation mails."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/refund.ts:25",
            "finding": "`refundOrder` refunds `order.subtotal` (the pre-discount amount) instead of `order.total` (what was paid), so discounted orders are over-refunded."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/api.ts:32",
            "finding": "`handleGetOrder` takes `query.customerId` but never checks it against `order.customer.id`, so any customer can read any order by guessing IDs such as `O1`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/admin.ts:38",
            "finding": "`adminRefund` passes `req.amount` to `issueRefund` unchecked, so negative, NaN, or above-total amounts are accepted. It does not consult `refundsOf`, so an order can be refunded repeatedly, and the audit entry is written before the refund succeeds."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CORRECTNESS",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/order.ts:101",
            "finding": "`markPaid` and `markFailed` set the status unconditionally, while `cancelOrder` is guarded. A late or replayed webhook can turn a cancelled order into \"paid\" with its stock already released, or flip a paid order to \"failed\"."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/api.ts:54",
            "finding": "The random-shuffle `recommendations` helper, together with the unused `ordersOf`, `refundsOf`, and `cancelOrder`, serves neither refunds nor payment webhooks. This is scope creep that adds dead, non-deterministic API surface."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "TESTING",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:1",
            "finding": "Security-sensitive logic (signature check, amount matching, admin gate, refund amounts, status transitions) has no tests. `README.md` still lists the old feature set and `package.json` is bumped to 1.6.0 with no changelog."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DESIGN",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:18",
            "finding": "`signaturesMatch` is a hand-rolled comparison instead of `crypto.timingSafeEqual`. `parseAmount` accepts \"\" as 0, and `parseEvent` does not validate the type of `amount`."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DESIGN",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/api.ts:43",
            "finding": "Two diverging refund paths now exist: `handleRefund` has no authorization and trusts the caller-supplied `Order.status`, while `adminRefund` has its own checks and calls `issueRefund` directly."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CLARITY",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:30",
            "finding": "The try/catch around the in-memory `outbox.push` can never fail, and its comment refers to an outbox retry job that does not exist, which misleads readers."
        }
    ]
}
```

